# Copy to .env.local for development. Production values belong in the host's
# environment settings (Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables),
# not in a file — SUBSCRIBE_TOKEN is a credential.


# The site's own origin, used to turn the share-card and Open Graph paths into
# absolute URLs. NEXT_PUBLIC_ means it is inlined into the client bundle at
# BUILD time, so changing it needs a rebuild, not just a restart.
#
# Without it these tags still render — they just point at localhost, which is
# right in development and wrong anywhere else: a link posted to Slack, X or
# WhatsApp shows no preview at all. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com


# Where the footer sign-up sends an address. app/api/subscribe/route.ts POSTs
#
#     {"email": "someone@example.com"}
#
# as application/json, and adds `Authorization: Bearer $SUBSCRIBE_TOKEN` when
# that is set.
#
# UNSET IS A DELIBERATE STATE, not an oversight: the route answers 503 and the
# footer says "Sign-up is not connected yet — nothing was saved." A form that
# thanks people and drops the address is worse, because nobody finds out until
# the list turns out to be empty.
#
# If the provider wants a different body — a Google Form wants form-encoded
# fields, Mailchimp wants status and merge_fields — that is the one thing in
# the route that has to change.
SUBSCRIBE_ENDPOINT=

# Only if the provider needs an Authorization header. Never commit a real one.
SUBSCRIBE_TOKEN=


# Where the speaker lineup and schedule come from. UNSET IS THE NORMAL CASE:
# the committed app/data.json is served, and editing means editing that file
# and deploying.
#
# Both point to tabs in the same Google Sheet. To set up:
#
#   1. In Sheets: File → Share → Publish to web.
#   2. Pick the speakers tab → CSV → Publish → copy the URL → SPEAKERS_URL.
#   3. Pick the schedule tab → CSV → Publish → copy the URL → SCHEDULE_URL.
#
# The feeds are re-read every five minutes, so a spreadsheet edit reaches the
# site within that without a deploy. If a fetch fails — unpublished, a renamed
# column, network down — the committed data is served instead and the reason
# is logged.
#
# Speaker images take either a direct link to an image file or a share link to
# a page holding one — an ImgBB or Google Photos link straight out of the Share
# button is resolved to the picture behind it. If that resolution fails, the
# card draws its placeholder and the reason is logged.
#
# Avoid formulas in the two published tabs. A formula that the publishing
# renderer cannot resolve puts #NAME? in the CSV instead of your data; the site
# retries, then falls back to app/data.json, so the page stays right but stops
# following the sheet. Generate what you like elsewhere and paste the result in
# with Edit > Paste special > Values only.
#
# The committed app/data.json is the fallback when a feed cannot be read, so it
# is worth keeping close to the sheet. To refresh it from the sheet and commit
# the result:
#
#   node --env-file=.env.local scripts/sync-data.mjs
SPEAKERS_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/EXAMPLE/pub?gid=SPEAKERS_TAB_GID&single=true&output=csv
SCHEDULE_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/EXAMPLE/pub?gid=SCHEDULE_TAB_GID&single=true&output=csv
